  m_Scene: {fileID: 102900000, guid: 5b5bedde531a61f47ae434cdaaa1cc5e, type: 3}
  m_ScenePath: Assets/Examples/Barrel/Barrel.unity
  m_ExampleName: Barrel
  m_Category: Benchmarks
  m_Description: A large barrel of various object types stress-testing the solver.
  m_Purpose: "A large barrel packed with a great many objects of one type, dropped in and left to settle.\nIt stress-tests the solver with a deep pile of touching bodies, so keep an eye on the frame rate in the Debug panel."
  m_Controls: "Object Type: chooses the type of object the barrel is filled with. The barrel refills when it changes.\nCollision Threshold: the body setting that decides when continuous collision is used. At zero it is always used. Whether a shape is using continuous collision detection (CCD) is shown by its color, which can be configured on the physics world. The barrel refills when it changes."
